---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Community Guidelines"
  description="Community Guidelines for Music Memory — rules for participating in our community features."
  canonical="/community-guidelines"
>
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-24" style="color: var(--ink-90)">
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold mb-8" style="color: var(--ink)">Community Guidelines</h1>

      <div class="space-y-8 glass p-8 rounded-3xl">
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-sm" style="color: var(--ink-90)">
          <strong>Effective Date:</strong> June 10, 2026
        </p>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--ink)">1. Purpose and Scope</h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed">
            These Community Guidelines (&ldquo;Guidelines&rdquo;) govern your participation in the community features of the Music Memory application. Community features include, but are not limited to: public journal entries, reactions (likes and dislikes), comments, replies, and feature requests. By using any community feature, you agree to abide by these Guidelines. These Guidelines supplement our Terms of Service and should be read in conjunction therewith.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--ink)">2. Community Principles</h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Music Memory is a platform for sharing the personal stories and emotions behind the music that shapes our lives. Our community is built upon the following principles:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2" style="color: var(--ink-90)">
            <li><strong>Authenticity:</strong> Share genuine memories and experiences connected to music.</li>
            <li><strong>Respect:</strong> Treat all community members with dignity and courtesy, regardless of their background, identity, or musical taste.</li>
            <li><strong>Safety:</strong> Maintain an environment where users feel comfortable sharing personal stories.</li>
            <li><strong>Privacy:</strong> Respect the personal nature of others&apos; memories and do not share or screenshot others&apos; content without consent.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--ink)">3. Content Standards</h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed mb-4">
            All publicly shared content must comply with the following standards:
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-3" style="color: var(--ink)">3.1 Permitted Content</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2" style="color: var(--ink-90)">
            <li>Personal memories, stories, and reflections associated with songs</li>
            <li>Photographs and videos that relate to your musical memories</li>
            <li>Constructive comments and reactions to others&apos; shared memories</li>
            <li>Location information relevant to where a musical memory took place</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-3" style="color: var(--ink)">3.2 Prohibited Content</h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The following content is strictly prohibited and will result in enforcement action:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2" style="color: var(--ink-90)">
            <li><strong>Hate Speech:</strong> Content that promotes hatred, discrimination, or violence against individuals or groups based on race, ethnicity, national origin, religion, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic.</li>
            <li><strong>Harassment and Bullying:</strong> Content intended to intimidate, threaten, demean, or target another individual, including repeated unwanted contact, personal attacks, or doxxing.</li>
            <li><strong>Sexually Explicit Material:</strong> Pornographic content, sexually explicit imagery, or content depicting sexual acts.</li>
            <li><strong>Violence and Graphic Content:</strong> Content that glorifies, promotes, or depicts gratuitous violence, gore, or self-harm.</li>
            <li><strong>Spam and Misleading Content:</strong> Repetitive, irrelevant, or deceptive content, including promotional material, phishing attempts, or content designed to manipulate engagement.</li>
            <li><strong>Illegal Activity:</strong> Content that promotes, facilitates, or depicts illegal activities, including drug use, theft, or fraud.</li>
            <li><strong>Intellectual Property Infringement:</strong> Content that infringes upon the copyrights, trademarks, or other intellectual property rights of third parties.</li>
            <li><strong>Personal Information:</strong> Sharing another person&apos;s private information (address, phone number, financial information) without their explicit consent.</li>
            <li><strong>Impersonation:</strong> Pretending to be another person, brand, or entity in a manner intended to deceive.</li>
            <li><strong>Misinformation:</strong> Deliberately false or misleading content that could cause harm.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--ink)">4. Interaction Standards</h2>

          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-3" style="color: var(--ink)">4.1 Comments and Replies</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2" style="color: var(--ink-90)">
            <li>Comments must be relevant to the memory or conversation</li>
            <li>Comments are limited to five hundred (500) characters</li>
            <li>Constructive feedback and genuine engagement are encouraged</li>
            <li>Personal attacks, insults, and derogatory language are prohibited</li>
            <li>Excessive commenting or spamming is prohibited</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-3" style="color: var(--ink)">4.2 Reactions</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2" style="color: var(--ink-90)">
            <li>Reactions (likes and dislikes) should reflect genuine sentiment</li>
            <li>Coordinated campaigns to mass-dislike a user&apos;s content are prohibited</li>
            <li>Using multiple accounts to manipulate reaction counts is prohibited</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-3" style="color: var(--ink)">4.3 Usernames and Profiles</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2" style="color: var(--ink-90)">
            <li>Usernames must not contain offensive, discriminatory, or misleading terms</li>
            <li>Usernames must not impersonate other individuals or entities</li>
            <li>Profile pictures must comply with the content standards outlined in Section 3</li>
            <li>Username changes are subject to a cooldown period to prevent abuse</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--ink)">5. Reporting and Moderation</h2>

          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-3" style="color: var(--ink)">5.1 Reporting Violations</h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If you encounter content or conduct that violates these Guidelines, you may report it using the flag icon. You can report a public entry, an individual comment, another user&apos;s profile, or another supported community item. When submitting a report, you will be asked to select a reason from the following categories:
          </p>
          <ul data-report-reasons class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2" style="color: var(--ink-90)">
            <li data-report-reason="harassment">Harassment or bullying</li>
            <li data-report-reason="hate_speech">Hate speech</li>
            <li data-report-reason="sexual_content">Sexual content</li>
            <li data-report-reason="violence_threats">Violence or threats</li>
            <li data-report-reason="self_harm">Self-harm</li>
            <li data-report-reason="spam_scam">Spam or scam</li>
            <li data-report-reason="impersonation">Impersonation</li>
            <li data-report-reason="copyright_ip">Copyright/IP</li>
            <li data-report-reason="personal_information">Personal information</li>
            <li data-report-reason="other">Other</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="leading-relaxed mt-4">
            Each user may submit one stored report for the same target. Duplicate report attempts do not create another stored report. False or malicious reporting is itself a violation of these Guidelines and may be reviewed.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-3" style="color: var(--ink)">5.2 Deterministic Prepublication Checks</h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Server-owned deterministic prepublication checks normalize public-facing text and apply the safety and anti-spam rules enforced by the Service before publication. Content that passes publishes immediately. Content that matches an enforced rule is not published, and the recorded decision can be appealed.
          </p>
          <p class="leading-relaxed">
            User reports are separate from those checks. A successful report immediately hides the reported target from the reporter, prevents another report from being stored for that same reporter and target, and creates or reuses a case for human review. A report by itself does not remove the target for everyone or impose an account action.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-3" style="color: var(--ink)">5.3 Human Review</h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed">
            An authorized human reviewer evaluates the case and may keep or restore the target, remove it, issue a warning, suspend access, or terminate an account when appropriate. Review decisions and appeals are recorded so the outcome is based on the reviewed content and conduct rather than on the number of reports received.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--ink)">6. Visibility and Access</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2" style="color: var(--ink-90)">
            <li>You choose the audience available for an entry: Only Me, Followers, or Public. New entries remain Only Me unless you affirmatively choose a shared audience.</li>
            <li>Your selected visibility remains unchanged unless you change it or an authorized human moderation decision changes the content&apos;s availability.</li>
            <li>Community entries for a given song are visible only to users who are otherwise allowed to view them under the Service&apos;s access rules.</li>
            <li>You may change a shared entry back to Only Me at any time.</li>
            <li>When you report a target, it is hidden from you immediately; that local hiding does not change what other users can see before review.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--ink)">7. Notifications</h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed">
            When you share content publicly, other users may interact with it. You will receive in-app notifications when someone likes your memory, comments on your entry, or replies to your comment. You may manage notification preferences through your device settings.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--ink)">8. Feature Requests</h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The feature request system allows users to suggest improvements and vote on others&apos; suggestions. When participating:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2" style="color: var(--ink-90)">
            <li>Feature requests must be constructive and relevant to the Service</li>
            <li>Duplicate requests should be avoided; vote on existing requests instead</li>
            <li>Feature requests that violate these Guidelines will be removed</li>
            <li>Submission of a feature request does not guarantee implementation</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--ink)">9. Consequences of Violations</h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed mb-4">
            After human review, a violation may result in one or more proportionate actions:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2" style="color: var(--ink-90)">
            <li>No action, or restoration of content, when the report is not substantiated</li>
            <li>Removal or restriction of specific content</li>
            <li>A warning</li>
            <li>Temporary suspension of community privileges</li>
            <li>Termination or banning of an account for severe or repeated violations</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="leading-relaxed mt-4">
            The outcome depends on the reviewed content, context, and conduct, not the number of reports. An authorized reviewer may take immediate action after review when a severe violation presents a safety or legal risk.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--ink)">10. Appeals</h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed">
            If you believe that enforcement action was taken against your account or content in error, you may contact us at <a href="mailto:support@musicmemory.app" class="hover:underline" style="color: var(--accent)">support@musicmemory.app</a> to request a review. Please include your username, a description of the content or action in question, and the reason you believe the action was taken in error. We will review appeals in good faith but are not obligated to reverse any enforcement decision.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--ink)">11. Changes to These Guidelines</h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed">
            We may update these Community Guidelines from time to time to reflect changes in our community standards or Service features. We will notify users of material changes by updating the &ldquo;Effective Date&rdquo; and, where practicable, by providing in-app notification. Your continued use of community features after changes are posted constitutes acceptance of the revised Guidelines.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4" style="color: var(--ink)">12. Contact</h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed">
            For questions about these Community Guidelines, to report violations, or to appeal enforcement actions, please contact us at:
          </p>
          <p class="leading-relaxed mt-2">
            Email: <a href="mailto:support@musicmemory.app" class="hover:underline" style="color: var(--accent)">support@musicmemory.app</a>
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>
